D=Path('/workspace/shared/nexus-usb-stack-review');p=json.loads((D/'geometry-evidence.json').read_text());f=D/'USB-STACK-REVIEW.md';s=f.read_text()
s=s.replace('For nearest main references, the center-projection lengths outside fill are:', 'For the outer-layer references and **both layers immediately adjacent to In3**, the center-projection lengths outside saved GND fill are:')
s=s.replace('| In3/In4 | 2.111 / 23.215 mm | 0.738 / 19.838 mm |', '| In3/In2 | 10.029 / 23.215 mm | 7.272 / 19.838 mm |\n| In3/In4 | 2.111 / 23.215 mm | 0.738 / 19.838 mm |')
start=s.index('**Every uncovered sample lies within 0.525 mm of a USB via.**')
end=s.index('\n\n## Declared stack',start)
s=s[:start]+'''For **In1/In4 only**, every uncovered center sample lies within 0.525 mm of a USB via; no unrelated mid-span fill gap was detected on those two references at this sampling resolution. Ordinary signal-via antipads are reference discontinuities, not evidence of a broad broken ground plane. The longest DP interval on those references is about 0.690 mm at x=108.152, y=127.028–127.718 around its off-center connector tee via.

**In2 also carries GND fill, interspersed with signal copper; it is not merely a signal-only layer.** Its closer fill covers 13.186 mm of DP and 12.566 mm of DM In3 centerline. It has uncovered center projections beyond the same USB-via neighborhoods: **7.190 mm DP and 5.816 mm DM**. Examples include DP x=110.575, y=113.105–114.595 (1.490 mm within one track) and DM near x=111.356–111.374, y=109.694–111.468 (1.774 mm within one track). Continuations across track endpoints can make a contiguous interval longer than an individual-record interval. At least one line-edge projection falls outside In2 GND for 10.759 mm DP / 7.792 mm DM. Thus a field model must account for changing adjacent copper and both In2/In4 references, rather than assign one uniform single-reference impedance. A mixed signal/GND layer is not automatically disqualified as a reference: assess its actual finite copper paths, coupling and GND interconnections.

Every segment/reference record enumerates the saved filled-polygon IDs touched by center and line-edge projections, expressed as zone UUID plus zero-based filled-polygon occurrence in the exact source:

- In1: `9f2a2d78-0e48-4414-9879-4fc68abc23e3:0`.
- In4: `88957e6f-e13e-4cbf-a8e2-1d52ff9863ab:0`.
- In2: zone `31ebd316-e294-41f0-8942-ba78a56019d4`, polygon indices **0, 2, 3 for DP** and **0, 1, 2, 3, 6 for DM**. Exact per-segment associations are in `geometry-evidence.json`. Multiple stored polygon memberships do not by themselves prove isolation; vias or other copper may connect them.

GND-via center distances range 0.710–2.538 mm from the seven signal vias; proximity alone does not prove a low-inductance return. Existing plated shield pads can provide additional returns and were not included in that nearest-via statistic. Finite return contact around each antipad/gap, via-to-plane copper contact and connections among these reference polygons/layers are **not proved** here and remain explicit native/geometric acceptance gates. These measurements are sampled projections, not a continuous return-current or EM analysis.''' +s[end:]
s=s.replace('The main GND planes are In1/In4. Outer traces have a 0.1164 mm dielectric to their nearest plane. In3 has **0.5500 mm to In4**, while the neighboring In2 signal layer is only **0.1532 mm** away. The current In3 route cannot use an outer-layer microstrip estimate. A proper In3 model would include both planes, layered dielectric and adjacent signal copper.', 'In1/In4 carry the principal GND pours. Outer traces have a 0.1164 mm dielectric to their neighboring GND layer. In3 has **0.5500 mm to In4** and only **0.1532 mm to In2**, which carries both GND fill and signal copper. Both adjacent layers are quantified above. The current In3 route cannot use an outer-layer microstrip estimate; a proper model includes the actual In2 and In4 copper, other significant conductors, layered dielectric and changing return geometry. An exclusively signal-free plane is not assumed necessary.')
s=s.replace('Its copper+dielectric sum is **1.6168 mm**, versus the general board thickness setting 1.6 mm; the two 0.010 mm masks are additional declared layers. Resolve that specification discrepancy with the fabricator before impedance release.', 'Its copper+dielectric sum is **1.6168 mm**, versus the nominal general board thickness setting 1.6 mm; the two 0.010 mm masks are additional declared layers. Confirm the intended production stack, finished copper/dielectric dimensions, nominal-thickness convention and tolerances with the fabricator before impedance release. This small nominal difference alone does **not** establish a fabrication defect.')
s=s.replace('seek a local duplicate join for each polarity, ideally roughly 2–3 mm A↔B planar connection, then a paired exit.', 'seek the shortest practical local duplicate join for each polarity, then a paired exit; quantify the resulting A↔B path and branches without imposing an unsupported length cap.')
s=s.replace('6. **Geometry goals, not compliance claims:** target ≤0.5 mm whole-port mismatch for **each orientation**, review any >1 mm residual; equal signal-via count and analogous transitions; no unrelated long branch/test pad; prefer total each-orientation planar path ≤35 mm without adding distant meanders just to match. These are conservative local engineering targets, not imported STM32 mandatory limits. Report unavoidable U7/connector uncoupled lengths separately.', '6. **Geometry goals:** minimize complete-port asymmetry and unnecessary branching for **each connector orientation**, use equal signal-via counts and analogous transitions where feasible, and avoid unrelated branch/test pads or distant meanders added merely to match length. Quantify each complete path by layer, barrel convention, branch and U7/connector uncoupled section, then compare against the current candidate. Do not impose arbitrary total-length or mismatch caps. Apply a numerical acceptance limit only when its applicability to this STM32 full-speed interface is established from the manufacturer or USB requirements; no such board-length/skew limit is established by this review.')
f.write_text(s)
(D/'analysis-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps({'source_sha256':p['board_sha256'],'summary':p['summary'],'paths':[{k:v for k,v in x.items() if k!='path'} for x in p['paths']]},indent=2)+'\n')
